  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **The World Is A Ghetto** (1 review): The reviewer says this song was dedicated to them, a cover they had awaited since following the band in 1999 [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **banter - what's up**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **banter - a special occasion**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **drum solo**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 10 archived performances [4]\n- **banter - inviting up Mark Whitfield on guitar**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **The World Is A Ghetto**: rare: 14 archived performances [4]\n- **banter - thanking Mark, inviting out Sam Kininger**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **banter - band intro, setbreak announce**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **banter - the new album**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2001-05-05.tlm170.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 27 songs; 172 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **soulive2001-05-05**: source not stated; 16 songs; 174 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: banter/encore break/pre-encore [1]\n- Played a very late-night set in the tiny House Of Blues Parish room during New Orleans Jazzfest, early in the band's career [1]\n- Sam Kininger joined the band on alto saxophone [2]\n- Uploader calls it a long, jammy show, with guitarist Mark Whitfield and Sam Kininger sitting in for substantial stretches [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2001-05-05.tlm170.flac16**: taped by Peter Costello & Scott Bernstein; transferred by Scott Bernstein; source: Onstage mics [1]. Also: Originally recorded by Peter Costello and Scott Bernstein; Bernstein transferred, mastered and tracked it between May 30 and June 3, 2010 [1]\n- **soulive2001-05-05**: taped by Kurt Ruthe; transferred by Kurt Ruthe; source: Schoeps MK21H > Schoeps KC5 > Schoeps VMS 52UB > Sonic AD2K+ > DAT (on stage) [2]",
